ordinates. The animateTransform on child rotates it around its local coords, parent transform applies afterwards. If child group's shapes centered at pedal location local coords (BB.x+38,BB.y), parent rotates around BB. The child's rotation axes rotate with parent, so counter rotation should offset parent orientation. For a horizontal pedal, child group shape maybe ellipse centered at local coords and rotate around that center with values 0 to -360. That works.\n\nBut animation phase relationship: wheel speed should match cranks visually? bicycling gearing: wheels turn ~2x cranks. We can set wheel 1.6s per revolution, crank 2.4s per revolution. Visually okay. Use 2.0s wheel, 3.0s crank? Cycle.\n\n3. Pelican body bob: slight translate y ±2, rotate around hip slight, 0.75s? Pedaling bob at 2x cadence maybe. Group with animateTransform translate values=\"0 0; 0 -3; 0 0\" dur=1.2 repeat indefinite. But if whole pelican including wings attached to moving handlebar? Wings should maybe remain on bars. If bob entire pelican, wing tips detach subtly. Small enough okay. Could animate torso only and legs separately. Neck/head bob.\n4. Wing \"elbow\" maybe small bob; hand on handlebar fixed. Maybe wings flap slightly but clutch bars, not needed.\n5. Legs pedaling: animate path d. Could do two legs: far leg dark orange, behind frame; near leg orange. Each path from hip to knee to foot/pedal position at sampled keyframes. But we need exact pedal positions to look connected. We can sample crank angle positions at times. Crank animation maybe 2.4s, starting right crank angle 0 (east). PedalR at BB + 38*(cos θ, sin θ). Left crank opposite. Hip around (550,390). Knee for bent leg. Need solve IK for leg segments lengths. We can approximate path with d values.\n\nLet's decide crank rotation direction: Bicycle moving right, wheels rotate clockwise. Cranks also rotate clockwise. In SVG y-axis down, clockwise rotation angle increasing (since angle from +x; positive angle rotates to +y). So values 0→360 for clockwise. Right pedal starts east (right) at θ=0, then south (down) at 90. Left pedal opposite θ=180. This means right foot down at 90.\n\nPelican legs: hip around maybe (565,380). The near leg (right) attaches to crank pedal at BB + 38*(cosθ,sinθ) but in side view th","truncated":true}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_kFqcfXsPrlqKOnHG159f6656","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport math\nH=(550,383); L1=106; L2=108; BB=(610,565); R=36\nfor deg in [0,45,90,135,180,225,270,315]:\n    P=(BB[0]+R*math.cos(math.radians(deg)), BB[1]+R*math.sin(math.radians(deg)))\n    dx=P[0]-H[0]; dy=P[1]-H[1]; d=math.hypot(dx,dy)\n    a=(L1*L1-L2*L2+d*d)/(2*d)\n    h=math.sqrt(max(0,L1*L1-a*a))\n    mx=H[0]+a*dx/d; my=H[1]+a*dy/d\n    k1=(mx - h*dy/d, my + h*dx/d)\n    k2=(mx + h*dy/d, my - h*dx/d)\n    print(deg, 'P', tuple(round(v) for v in P),'d',round(d,1), 'K1',tuple(round(v) for v in k1), 'K2',tuple(round(v) for v in k2))\nPY","description":"Calculate leg IK knee positions"}}
