{"type":"thinking","text":"No xmllint. Can parse XML with Python.\n\nNow writing. To manage leg path values, generate via Python. Let's define leg path strings with samples. Use path M Hx Hy L Kx Ky L Px Py. Hip maybe 550,398. For near and far. Use smooth interpolation? Linear between 24 samples looks fine at 2.4s, but knee may jitter due IK branch; for all angles branch K2 consistent. Could use N=32. Values length ~32*30 chars = 1KB each. Fine.\n\nNeed ensure at t=0 and t=1 same values for seamless loop. Angle 360 same as 0; include final. KeyTimes 0..1. Dur 2.4. For near, angle 0 to 360. For far, 180 to 540. For crank groups, both 0→360 with far arm opposite. Sync.\n\nPedal foot orientation counter-rotation: foot rotates -360 over 2.4. But because it's a full rotation, same. The foot will always stay horizontal in world space. Good.\n\nBut the foot center (pedal) itself rotates around BB, and the group has translate with rotating parent. Counter-rotation in local coordinate cancels orientation. Good.\n\nDo we want the foot rotated slightly to match ankle? Foot flat horizontal looks good on pedal. Add ankle shape near top-left.\n\nNear leg path ends at pedal center (646,565). Foot shape centered at 646,565 can overlap. We need draw near leg before near crank group so foot overlays path end. Fine.\n\nFar leg end at far pedal 574,565. Far foot in far crank group behind frame. Good.\n\nWheels:\nUse 12 spokes perhaps; rotation visible. Each wheel:\n```\n<g id=rear-spin>\n <animateTransform .../>\n <g stroke=...> line x1=390 y1=425 x2=390 y2=665? But radius 120: from center top to bottom etc.\n``` \nUse line pairs across diameter at angles 0,30,60,90,120,150 => 12 spokes (6 diameters).\nCoordinates for center (390,545), radius 118:\nx = cx + r cos; etc. Could generate static lines.\nAdd small gold nipples at radius 112 maybe.\nReflector at (390+55,545+95) perhaps.\nHub circle static should not rotate visually (symmetric) but okay inside.\nTire circle static separate from spinner. Rim circle static. Spokes animate within.\nMaybe add rotating valve stem at (390,427) small red dot.\n\nFenders? Let's decide. A classy bike with teal frame, cream tires maybe. We can add partial fenders (mudguards) in cream over rear/front wheels. But fender covers top and spokes still visible lower. It adds visual interest. However fenders must be static and drawn behind frame? Fenders usually above wheel. Draw after wheel, before frame. Use arc:\nRear fender path: `M 274 510 A 136 136 0 0 1 506 510` with stroke #E8D9BC width=10 linecap=round. But endpoints maybe. Arc radius 136 around (390,545), at x=274 dx=-116, dy=-35 => y=510. Top y=409. So fender arcs over top. That's a lot of cream band. It will cover upper spokes. Fine. Add small red rear reflector at fender end? Maybe.\nFront fender similar `M 734 510 A 136 136 0 0 1 966 510`.\nBut the frame seat stays/top tube cross. Fenders behind frame. Good. Could make fenders teal darker with cream pinstripe, matching bike. Let's use `#E7D7B8` stroke width 7 plus thin center line teal opacity? Hmm. Cream fenders pop on teal.\n\nMaybe skip fenders to keep clean and wheel spin visible. I think classic fenders enhance. Let's include front small fender only? Bicycle uncluttered. Let's render and see.\n\nPelican body drawing:\nLet's create path with smooth shape. Body:\n```\n<path d=\"M 502 353\n C 490 323 509 293 540 278\n C 573 262 612 270 636 294\n C 664 322 664 358 646 382\n C 625 409 584 411 551 397\n C 523 385 512 372 502 353 Z\" fill=url(#bodyGrad) stroke=#CBD8D4 width=2/>\n```\nBody center around 575,340. Saddle at 500,385; body bottom 400. Good.\nTail feathers extend left from 507,345: shape M 515 341 L 450 322 L 463 347 L 440 355 L 466 359 L 455 376 L 505 368... fill cream. Maybe tail behind body. Draw before body.\nWing near as described. Belly shadow path.\nChest maybe extends right to 650. Neck starts at 630,295.\nNeck thick stroke at (620,300) to (720,190).\nLet's set body top 275 and neck:\n`M 620 303 C 618 263 650 250 674 225 C 690 209 706 194 726 188`\nstroke white 46, linecap round. This might blend into head. Add a neck shadow thin path on left `M 610 300 C 610 263 641 249 665 225...` stroke #D8E2DE width 5 opacity.\nHead shape: ellipse centered (738,182) rx=37 ry=33, rotate -10. Plus crown/crest:\n`M 714 158 C 716 142 730 143 734 152 C 737 140 749 139 754 149 C 760 142 770 148 770 158` maybe soft crest, fill #F4F0E2.\nHead outline subtle stroke #CBD8D4.\nEye at (744,172). Beak attaches at x=770.\nActually head front x=775. Beak origin around 765. Good.\n\nNeck-body attachment at (620,303), body chest x=650 y=310. Wing shoulder maybe 590,300.\n\nWing:\nNeed distinctly a wing not arm. Shape broad near shoulder then tapers to handlebar. \n```\n<path d=\"M 558 296\n C 592 277 628 288 656 315\n C 674 333 697 348 727 356\n C 749 362 770 361 787 364\n L 796 374\n C 780 386 754 388 729 381\n C 695 372 665 356 643 337\n C 622 318 594 314 560 327\n C 546 321 546 304 558 296 Z\" fill=url(#wingGrad) stroke=#BCCBC6/>\n```\nTip near (796,374), gripping bar at (785,363). Add black primaries:\n`M 745 372 C 760 379 775 384 792 383 L 788 392 C 769 391 750 385 736 377 Z` fill #25343B, and another feather. This will be at wing lower edge near bar, nice.\nMaybe near wing should be much larger, with folded elbow high. Pelican wing while reaching handlebar could be like a long curved arm. This shape is okay. Add 4 feather lines along wing:\n`M 596 304 C 618 306 639 323 654 338`, etc.\nBlack tips at bottom near handlebar.\n\nFar wing behind body:\n`M 566 288 C 620 278 674 307 710 339 C 730 357 756 365 782 361 L 789 369 C 760 382 718 377 686 356 C 650 333 609 316 560 329 Z` fill #CFDBD7. It may be visible behind body and near wing, extending to (789,369). Add black tips maybe.\nLayer order: far wing drawn before torso? It is on far side, should be behind body. Draw far wing first, then torso, then near wing. Neck maybe after far wing but before near wing? Head should be front. Fine.\n\nTail: draw before body. Tail feathers perhaps sticking back-left from hip. Use 3 overlapping pointed feather shapes:\n`M 520 340 C 490 318 468 306 450 300 C 466 320 476 331 487 340 C 470 341 454 338 442 334 C 464 350 486 357 510 360 Z` fill #F7F1E4.\nCould be behind body.\n\nScarf: Add neck scarf around base of neck at (640,244)? Actually scarf around neck around y=255. orange. Shape follows neck:\n`M 624 278 C 635 286 653 282 662 268 C 669 256 669 244 660 237 C 652 247 645 257 633 261 Z` fill #E76F51. Tails behind left:\n`M 632 262 C 596 252 574 269 532 253 C 548 277 585 292 624 279 Z` fill #E76F51. Animate d with wave. But if scarf tails go over far wing? Scarf is on near side of neck, tails back over body/wing. Draw after torso and wings maybe to be visible. However neck should overlay scarf maybe. Draw scarf after neck and near wing, before head? Tails can fly over back. Put scarf on top after body/wing/neck. The knot around neck overlays neck lower part. That looks natural. Head separate on top.\n\nNeed animate scarf path d. Values:\nA: M 632 262 C 596 252 574 269 532 253 C 548 277 585 292 624 279 Z\nB: M 632 262 C 596 247 571 252 526 233 C 546 262 580 284 624 279 Z\nC: M 632 262 C 598 255 579 263 538 243 C 552 270 586 289 624 279 Z\nAnimate A→B→C→A dur 1.1s. KeyTimes 0;.33;.66;1. Linear. This is visible.\nMaybe two tail ribbons with second thinner darker orange. Could add after main scarf with separate wave. Keep one.\n\nHead crest feathers at back: 3 small strokes.\n\nBeak pouch detail lines.\n\nColors:\n- white body #FBF8EF\n- white shading #E6EDE8\n- outline #B9C8C3 (soft)\n- wing shade #D6E2DD\n- black primaries #2B3940\n- beak upper #F4A259\n- beak shadow #E07A3F\n- pouch #E76F51, highlight #F2A07F\n- legs #E79A3B, outline #B8682B\n- scarf #D9553F / #F07A5A\n- saddle #6A4B3A\n- frame #1F6264 / highlight #3D8B85\n- gold #D9A45B\n- tires #253238.\n\nBackground:\nsky gradient #A8D5D8 (top) to #F8E7C8 (bottom).\nsun #FFD18A.\nhills: back #88B7A8, front #6C9F8F, distant #A7C8BA.\nroad #D9BE98, top edge #EFE0C5, dashes #F8EDD9.\ngrass #8CAE72 accents.\nClouds cream.\n\nNeed subtle texture maybe pattern of grass.\n\nLet's create SVG using Python for leg value strings. Maybe also generate spokes. Write a script to create final; then inspect and refine via edits. Since final only needs pelican.sv","truncated":true}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_L9WK8XXBStEuYVF8yCUg2007","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/gen_pelican.py <<'PY'\nimport math\n\ndef ik_path(hip, L1, L2, target):\n    Hx, Hy = hip\n    Px, Py = target\n    dx, dy = Px-Hx, Py-Hy\n    d = math.hypot(dx, dy)\n    d = min(d, L1+L2-0.01)\n    a = (L1*L1 - L2*L2 + d*d)/(2*d)\n    h = math.sqrt(max(0.0, L1*L1 - a*a))\n    mx, my = Hx + a*dx/d, Hy + a*dy/d\n    # knee points forward/up (right side of hip->pedal vector)\n    kx = mx + h*dy/d\n    ky = my - h*dx/d\n    return f\"M {Hx:.1f} {Hy:.1f} L {kx:.1f} {ky:.1f} L {Px:.1f} {Py:.1f}\"\n\nBB = (610.0, 565.0)\nR = 36.0\nHn = (550.0, 398.0)\nHf = (538.0, 394.0)\nnear, far = [], []\nN = 48\nfor i in range(N+1):\n    t = i/N\n    th = 2*math.pi*t\n    Pn = (BB[0]+R*math.cos(th), BB[1]+R*math.sin(th))\n    Pf = (BB[0]+R*math.cos(th+math.pi), BB[1]+R*math.sin(th+math.pi))\n    near.append(ik_path(Hn, 108, 113, Pn))\n    far.append(ik_path(Hf, 106, 111, Pf))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    print('NEAR_VALUES=\"' + ';'.join(near) + '\"')\n    print('FAR_VALUES=\"' + ';'.join(far) + '\"')\nPY\npython3 /tmp/gen_pelican.py | head -c 500","description":"Generate animated leg path keyframes"}}
