{"type":"thinking","text":"Good. Need maybe foot target at pedal center but foot foot maybe on pedal top; target y=565 means ankle at center, foot flat across. okay.\n\nNow write SVG. We could use Python to output. Let's craft carefully.\n\nColors/design in full.\n\nSVG skeleton:\n\n```\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 800\" fill=\"none\">\n<title>Pelican riding a bicycle</title>\n<desc>A white pelican ...</desc>\n<defs>\n <linearGradient id=\"sky\" ...>\n ...\n <radialGradient id=\"sunGlow\">...\n <linearGradient id=\"bodyFill\">\n ...\n <linearGradient id=\"wingFill\">\n <linearGradient id=\"hillBack\"...\n <linearGradient id=\"roadFill\"...\n <filter id=\"blur18\"...>\n</defs>\n<rect ... />\n<g id=\"background\">...</g>\n...\n</svg>\n```\n\nNeed CSS maybe no. Use attributes.\n\nSky: #A9D4D8 to #F7E4C3. Maybe top a bit deeper for contrast: #8EC6CC -> #D6E8DC -> #F8E3C1. 3 stops.\n\nSun glow: radial gradient #FFE2A6 opacity. filter blur maybe. Circle at (975,150) r=160 fill url(#sunGlow) opacity .65, plus core r=64 fill #FFD487. Add rotating? No.\nClouds: soft cream with opacity .7. Use paths with round shapes. Add drift animateTransform to each group around subtle ±10. Use `<animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0; -16 4; 0 0\" dur=\"14s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>` but if group uses transform? Put animate inside group no transform. Multiple with different dur. Good. Note if multiple clouds in one group with animate, all move together; okay.\n\nHills:\n- Back layer: path from 0,560 C 120 500, 230 490, 330 545 C 430 600? Let's create rolling hills. Or simple large ellipses. A path:\n`M 0 590 C 120 515 220 505 330 555 C 410 590 470 570 560 540 C 660 505 760 500 860 550 C 950 595 1050 570 1200 505 L 1200 680 L 0 680 Z` fill #7DAD9F.\n- Front layer:\n`M 0 620 C 120 580 230 575 340 610 C 460 646 580 605 690 585 C 810 563 925 580 1030 615 C 1100 637 1150 632 1200 620 L 1200 680 L 0 680 Z` fill #6B9D8C.\nBut bike at y=680; hills should be behind road which starts 645. So foreground hills bottoms behind road. Good.\n- Add little tree silhouettes? Maybe a few minimal bushes/trees at x=120,y=580 etc. Could add simple trunks and round tops, but focus. Maybe add distant birds (V shapes) in sky to fill. Small.\n\nRoad: rect y=640 height=160 fill #D8BC92; top highlight line y=640 h=8 #EAD6B4; maybe edge. dashed center line at y=723 with dash 46 gap 66, animate translate. Add gravel dots.\n\nBike shadow ellipse around (620,684), rx 360 ry 14 fill #6A5A45 opacity .18; animated rx? maybe subtle.\nSpeed lines behind: 4 horizontal rounded paths at y=320,400,470 x 100-220 with opacity .25, animate translate left maybe. They reinforce riding. But background hills etc. Could add small teal and cream streaks. Use `stroke-linecap round`. Maybe z-order behind bike.\n\nWheel:\nTire outer circle r=134, stroke #26343A width 12, fill none. Add subtle highlight arc top left #44545A width 3 opacity .6.\nRim circle r=119, stroke #D7B179 width 4.5. Inner rim r=112? Spokes from center to r=112.\nTire sidewall ring r=126, stroke #F1E7D6 width 2 opacity .3? maybe.\nAnimated spinner group:\n```\n<g>\n <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" from=\"0 390 545\" to=\"360 390 545\" dur=\"1.45s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n <g stroke=\"#F7EEDC\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" opacity=\".85\" stroke-linecap=\"round\">\n  lines...\n </g>\n <circle cx=... r=5 fill gold/>\n <circle cx=... r=4 fill coral/> reflector\n</g>\n```\n16 spokes (8 diameters) yields more blur. Use 12 spokes. Reflector at 390+78? The spokes rotating; reflector gold/coral circle.\nAdd hub outer circle r=14 fill #2E3A3F stroke #D7B179 width 3, center r=5 gold. Hub static drawn after spinner. Tire/rim static before spinner. For wheel spin visual, reflector moves. Good.\nPotential problem spinner animation around center if from/to formatting. Use `values=\"0 390 545;360 390 545\"`.\n\nWheels drawn twice with different centers but shared markup manually.\n\nFender:\nMaybe draw rear fender after wheel: path `M 270 515 A 135 135 0 0 1 510 515` stroke #E6D4B3 width 9 fill none stroke-linecap round. Arrow? But arc ends below top. Add small red light at arc end x=272,y=515 maybe. Front similar. However fender path over top wheel might intersect frame nicely. Include.\n\nChain:\nRear cog at (390,545) r=14, drawn spinner maybe. Chain top line from 390,531 to 610,535; bottom 390,559 to 610,595. Use path with lines and arcs:\n```\n<path d=\"M 390 531 L 610 535 A 30 30 0 0 1 610 595 L 390 559 A 14 14 0 0 1 390 531 Z\" fill=none stroke=#4B5A5E stroke-width=3 stroke-dasharray=\"7 5\">\n <animate attributeName=\"stroke-dashoffset\" from=\"0\" to=\"-48\" dur=\"0.6s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n</path>\n```\nWait path direction and arc. Chainring circle top at 535, bottom 595. Arc from top to bottom on right side radius 30 going clockwise? `A 30 30 0 0 1 610 595` sweeps right side, yes. Then line to rear bottom (390,559), then arc around rear cog from bottom to top on left side: starting (390,559) to (390,531), with A 14 14 0 0 1? In SVG y down, arc sweep 1 means clockwise from bottom to top goes left side? From (390,559) to (390,531), center 390,545. Clockwise direction from angle 90° to 270° goes through 180° (left). Yes sweep=1 goes clockwise? In SVG, sweep-flag 1 means positive-angle direction; angle increases clockwise on screen due y down. From bottom (90°) increasing to 270° passes left (180°). So left side. Good. Path closed. Animate dashoffset negative for chain movement maybe direction. Fine.\nBut chain should be behind frame and chainring. Draw after wheels before frame. Rear cog included in spinner? Keep rear cog drawn static in chain group with gold fill and ring. Add spinner cog separately maybe. A rotating 14-tooth cog not visible; okay.\n\nFar crank group behind frame:\n```\n<g id=\"far-crank\">\n <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0 610 565;360 610 565\" dur=\"2.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n <line x1=\"610\" y1=\"565\" x2=\"574\" y2=\"565\" stroke=\"#D7CFC1\" width=8 />\n <g transform=\"translate(574 565)\">\n   <g>\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0;-360\" dur=\"2.4s\".../>\n    <rect x=-18 y=3 width=36 height=6 rx=3 fill=\"#3B474B\"/>\n    far foot...\n   </g>\n </g>\n</g>\n```\nFoot shape path in local:\n`M -18 -7 C -12 -14 2 -15 9 -8 L 18 -2 L 8 2 C 0 -2 -8 0 -16 3 C -20 1 -21 -3 -18 -7 Z`\nWait foot should be webbed, pointing right. Pedal from -18 to 18 horizontally. Foot from -15 to 22, toes. Add 2 webbed lobes. Use fill orange stroke darker. Let's define foot path:\n`M -14 -4 C -8 -10 4 -10 10 -5 L 23 -1 L 11 2 C 7 -1 2 0 -2 2 L -8 7 L -12 2 C -17 2 -18 -1 -14 -4 Z`\nThis produces three toe points maybe. Simpler:\n`M -13 -5 C -7 -11 3 -10 9 -5 L 22 -2 C 13 3 3 3 -5 1 L -11 7 C -16 4 -17 -1 -13 -5 Z`\nLooks like webbed foot with pointed toe to right. Good.\nAdd foot outline stroke #A85C27 width 2. Add webbing line.\n\nNear crank group after frame and near leg? Contains chainring? Need layering:\n- far leg before frame\n- far crank before frame\n- chain\n- frame\n- near leg (in front of frame)\n- near crank/pedal (in front of near leg)\n- maybe chainring should be behind near leg but in front of frame. Could include chainring in near crank group, which overlays near leg? Chainring at BB radius30, near leg lower part around x640,y520 maybe not overlapping much. If chainring drawn in front of near leg, bad if leg crosses ring? Near leg from knee 643,452 to pedal 646,565 passes just right of chainring (x 640) and could overlay chainring. Natural near leg should be in front of chainring. So draw chainring before near leg, crank arm and pedal after near leg.\nStructure:\n- chainring group (rotating) at BB with gold ring and spider; drawn after frame.\n- near leg.\n- near crank arms/pedals group rotating, drawn after.\nBut near crank group animation and chainring separate both rotate same; fine.\nHowever near crank group includes far? no.\n- Feet on pedals in near crank group.\n\nNear leg ends at pedal center; foot overlays. Good.\n\nFrame draw with seatpost, handlebar. Fenders maybe behind frame.\n\nBike details:\n- bottle cage? Maybe skip.\n- Handlebar grips dark.\n- Bell gold small at handlebar.\n- Headlamp? Maybe add small cream lamp at front head tube; could","truncated":true}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_FZnVsFiyaY2T2YKEADuM3760","tool":"bash","input":{"command":"cat > /tmp/build_pelican.py <<'PY'\nimport math\n\n# ---------- animated leg geometry ----------\ndef ik_path(hip, L1, L2, target):\n    Hx, Hy = hip\n    Px, Py = target\n    dx, dy = Px-Hx, Py-Hy\n    d = math.hypot(dx, dy)\n    d = min(d, L1+L2-0.01)\n    a = (L1*L1 - L2*L2 + d*d)/(2*d)\n    h = math.sqrt(max(0.0, L1*L1 - a*a))\n    mx, my = Hx + a*dx/d, Hy + a*dy/d\n    kx = mx + h*dy/d\n    ky = my - h*dx/d\n    return f\"M {Hx:.1f} {Hy:.1f} L {kx:.1f} {ky:.1f} L {Px:.1f} {Py:.1f}\"\n\nBB = (610.0, 565.0)\nR = 36.0\nHn = (550.0, 398.0)\nHf = (538.0, 394.0)\nnear, far = [], []\nN = 48\nfor i in range(N+1):\n    t = i/N\n    th = 2*math.pi*t\n    Pn = (BB[0]+R*math.cos(th), BB[1]+R*math.sin(th))\n    Pf = (BB[0]+R*math.cos(th+math.pi), BB[1]+R*math.sin(th+math.pi))\n    near.append(ik_path(Hn, 108, 113, Pn))\n    far.append(ik_path(Hf, 106, 111, Pf))\nNEAR_VALUES = ';'.join(near)\nFAR_VALUES = ';'.join(far)\n\n# ---------- wheel spokes ----------\ndef spokes(cx, cy, r=112):\n    out = []\n    for k in range(6):\n        ang = math.radians(k*30)\n        dx, dy = r*math.cos(ang), r*math.sin(ang)\n        out.append(f'<line x1=\"{cx-dx:.1f}\" y1=\"{cy-dy:.1f}\" x2=\"{cx+dx:.1f}\" y2=\"{cy+dy:.1f}\"/>')\n    return '\\n          '.join(out)\n\nREAR_SPOKES = spokes(390,545)\nFRONT_SPOKES = spokes(850,545)\n\n# ---------- road dashes ----------\nDASHES = '\\n        '.join(\n    f'<line x1=\"{x}\" y1=\"738\" x2=\"{x+82}\" y2=\"738\"/>' for x in range(-210, 1300, 170)\n)\n\nsvg = f'''<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1200\" height=\"800\" viewBox=\"0 0 1200 800\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"title desc\">\n  <title id=\"title\">Pelican riding a bicycle</title>\n  <desc id=\"desc\">A cheerful white pelican in a red scarf rides a teal bicycle. It sits on the saddle, grips the handlebars with its wings, and pedals as the wheels and cranks turn.</desc>\n  <defs>\n    <linearGradient id=\"sky\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#83bfc8\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"0.55\" stop-color=\"#c7e2db\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#f8e4c3\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n    <radialGradient id=\"sunGlow\" cx=\"50%\" cy=\"50%\" r=\"50%\">\n      <stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#ffdf9d\" stop-opacity=\"0.95\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"0.45\" stop-color=\"#ffdda0\" stop-opacity=\"0.35\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#ffdda0\" stop-opacity=\"0\"/>\n    </radialGradient>\n    <linearGradient id=\"hillBack\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#8bb8a9\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#76a797\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n    <linearGradient id=\"hillFront\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#6f9f8d\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#5d8b7c\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n    <linearGradient id=\"road\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#dfc7a2\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"0.35\" stop-color=\"#d8bd96\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#c8a97e\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n    <linearGradient id=\"bodyFill\" x1=\"0.2\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0.75\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#fffdf7\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"0.55\" stop-color=\"#faf6ea\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#e8eee7\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n    <linearGradient id=\"wingFill\" x1=\"0.1\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0.9\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#fbf9f1\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"0.6\" stop-color=\"#e4ebe4\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#cfdcd6\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n    <linearGradient id=\"farWingFill\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"0.7\">\n      <stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#dbe5df\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#bccdc7\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n    <linearGradient id=\"beakFill\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"0.25\">\n      <stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#f8b66b\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"0.7\" stop-color=\"#f0a052\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#e88d43\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n    <linearGradient id=\"pouchFill\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0.3\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#ef8158\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#dd5e42\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n    <radialGradient id=\"shadowGrad\" cx=\"50%\" cy=\"50%\" r=\"50%\">\n      <stop offset=\"0\" stop-color=\"#5d4d38\" stop-opacity=\"0.28\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#5d4d38\" stop-opacity=\"0\"/>\n    </radialGradient>\n    <filter id=\"blurSoft\" x=\"-50%\" y=\"-50%\" width=\"200%\" height=\"200%\">\n      <feGaussianBlur stdDeviation=\"9\"/>\n    </filter>\n  </defs>\n\n  <!-- sky and sun -->\n  <rect width=\"1200\" height=\"800\" fill=\"url(#sky)\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"979\" cy=\"151\" r=\"165\" fill=\"url(#sunGlow)\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"979\" cy=\"151\" r=\"60\" fill=\"#ffd68b\" opacity=\"0.95\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"979\" cy=\"151\" r=\"60\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ffe6b2\" stroke-width=\"3\" opacity=\"0.7\"/>\n\n  <!-- clouds -->\n  <g fill=\"#fffaf0\" opacity=\"0.8\">\n    <g>\n      <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-18 3;0 0\" dur=\"17s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n      <path d=\"M 120 175 C 128 146 168 143 180 165 C 193 146 229 149 235 173 C 257 169 271 184 267 201 L 125 201 C 112 199 106 183 120 175 Z\"/>\n    </g>\n    <g opacity=\"0.72\">\n      <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;14 2;0 0\" dur=\"21s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n      <path d=\"M 500 118 C 507 96 538 94 548 111 C 558 96 584 99 589 117 C 608 114 617 126 613 140 L 505 140 C 493 138 490 126 500 118 Z\"/>\n    </g>\n    <g opacity=\"0.6\">\n      <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-13 2;0 0\" dur=\"15s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n      <path d=\"M 804 245 C 811 226 838 224 847 239 C 856 226 878 229 883 244 C 898 242 907 253 903 264 L 809 264 C 799 262 796 252 804 245 Z\"/>\n    </g>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- distant birds -->\n  <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#456f70\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0.42\">\n    <path d=\"M 318 228 C 326 220 333 220 340 226 C 347 220 354 220 361 228\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 374 203 C 380 197 385 197 390 202 C 395 197 401 197 406 203\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 285 262 C 290 257 295 257 299 261 C 303 257 308 257 313 262\"/>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- hills -->\n  <path d=\"M 0 596 C 95 531 185 512 287 551 C 385 589 454 590 557 548 C 659 507 755 505 856 556 C 959 608 1070 586 1200 512 L 1200 700 L 0 700 Z\" fill=\"url(#hillBack)\"/>\n  <path d=\"M 0 622 C 115 581 217 580 326 616 C 438 653 546 620 656 590 C 765 561 880 576 987 611 C 1091 645 1155 634 1200 622 L 1200 700 L 0 700 Z\" fill=\"url(#hillFront)\"/>\n\n  <!-- little shrubs on the hillside -->\n  <g fill=\"#4f7b6b\" opacity=\"0.55\">\n    <path d=\"M 87 625 C 83 610 94 601 105 607 C 110 593 129 595 132 610 C 145 607 151 619 146 626 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 173 638 C 169 626 179 618 188 623 C 193 612 208 614 211 626 C 221 624 226 633 222 639 Z\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 1060 624 C 1056 610 1068 602 1078 608 C 1083 595 1100 597 1103 611 C 1116 608 1122 620 1117 626 Z\"/>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- road -->\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"650\" width=\"1200\" height=\"150\" fill=\"url(#road)\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"650\" width=\"1200\" height=\"7\" fill=\"#f0dfbf\" opacity=\"0.8\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#f8ebd3\" stroke-width=\"7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0.72\">\n    <g>\n      <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-170 0\" dur=\"1.35s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n      {DASHES}\n    </g>\n  </g>\n  <g fill=\"#ac8d65\" opacity=\"0.4\">\n    <circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"704\" r=\"2.2\"/><circle cx=\"213\" cy=\"688\" r=\"1.7\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"362\" cy=\"757\" r=\"2.4\"/><circle cx=\"503\" cy=\"711\" r=\"1.8\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"739\" cy=\"780\" r=\"2.1\"/><circle cx=\"900\" cy=\"700\" r=\"1.6\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"1089\" cy=\"760\" r=\"2.3\"/><circle cx=\"1150\" cy=\"690\" r=\"1.7\"/>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- speed streaks -->\n  <g stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0.35\">\n    <g stroke=\"#f9edda\" stroke-width=\"5\">\n      <line x1=\"140\" y1=\"445\" x2=\"225\" y2=\"445\">\n        <animate attributeName=\"x1\" values=\"140;100;140\" dur=\"3s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n        <animate attributeName=\"x2\" values=\"225;185;225\" dur=\"3s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n      </line>\n      <line x1=\"115\" y1=\"497\" x2=\"205\" y2=\"497\">\n        <animate attributeName=\"x1\" values=\"115;80;115\" dur=\"3.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n        <animate attributeName=\"x2\" values=\"205;170;205\" dur=\"3.4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>\n      </line>\n    </g>\n    <g stroke=\"#286b6d\" stroke-width=\"4\" opacity=\"0.5\">\n      <line x1=\"230\" y1=\"378\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"378\">\n        <animate attributeName=\"x1\" values","description":"Generate SVG and render preview"},"truncated":true}
